            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous pneumomediastinum in H1N1 infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>976-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous pneumomediastinum is an uncommon pediatric emergency which usually occurs secondary to bronchial asthma in children. We report a case of spontaneous pneumomediastinum in a 7 year child following Swine Flu (H1N1) infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
